#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Create the folio repository with `bun run init-folio` (or the folio_init tool): content/, the document, chapter and first block manifests, the builder shim, AGENTS.md, .mcp.json, the session-start hook and the beans store, with the platform linked rather than copied."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:106
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every block edit runs the HCI validation gate — see editing-hci-validation.bpmn."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:26
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "folio-assistant — authoring a scientific paper end to end (Lean + LaTeX). Source of truth: this file. Open it in bpmn.io, Camunda Modeler, or any other BPMN 2.0 tool. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The <folio:skill> extension on an activity names the folio-assistant skill that implements it; <folio:bean> marks a step that reads or writes the shared work plan in beans/."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Gateway_ReviewOutcome sits in this lane rather than a separate editor's, so in this diagram the reviewer's finding and its disposition are the same decision — iterate back to Task_AuthorBlocks or clear Task_Publish — because paper authoring has no editor lane to hold the accept/reject split modelled elsewhere in this corpus."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:115
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Give each formal block (definition, theorem, lemma, proposition, corollary, conjecture, proof) a .lean sibling that Lean 4 accepts, in the order lean-formalization sets out. A compiling declaration is not a formalised claim: check vacuity and narrative drift before calling it done, and record the status with proof-verification."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:181
#. Diagram label
msgid "green"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:185
#. Diagram label
msgid "iterate"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:63
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Its three tasks bracket the human review rather than replace it: Validate and Render turn the Lean-green manuscript into the artefact Task_Review actually reads, and Publish only fires once Gateway_ReviewOutcome has said 'approved' — this lane builds what gets judged and executes what was decided, and decides nothing itself."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:56
#. Diagram label
msgid "Lean toolchain (lean-mcp)"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:77
#. Diagram label
msgid "New paper"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:180
#. Diagram label
msgid "not yet"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:57
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Owns its own loop: Gateway_LeanGreen's 'not yet' branch returns straight to Task_Formalize rather than out to a person, and the gateway itself is DMN-computed off the build result rather than argued, so nothing downstream can proceed on a proof that merely looks close enough. The paper does not reach Task_Validate until this lane's own gate says green."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:171
#. Diagram label
msgid "Paper published"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:157
#. Diagram label
msgid "Ready to publish?"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:150
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Review the rendered paper, not a description of it, and record the feedback. The outcome is iterate — back to authoring — or approved for the publication path."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reviewer / SME"
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:134
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Run content validation over the folio: schemas, the content profile (formal kinds only in a paper), cross-block consistency and that the Lean builds. Loop back rather than rendering over a failure."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:51
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Scaffolds the repo from the author's plan and then writes every block — including every revision, since Gateway_ReviewOutcome's 'iterate' branch re-enters Task_AuthorBlocks directly rather than sending the change back to Lane_Author to be re-scoped. The plan is the author's decision; executing against it, first draft through every rewrite, is this lane's."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:81
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Scope the paper: chapters, the blocks each needs, what gets formalised."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:164
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "See draft-to-publication.bpmn for the review and release path this expands into."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:46
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Sits between Task_Plan and Task_Scaffold as the one conversion point in this diagram: the author's plan becomes beans here, which is what lets a resumed session or a different agent pick up Task_Scaffold without having sat through Task_Plan itself."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:89
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The plan becomes beans, so a resumed session or a sibling agent can pick it up."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:40
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The plan set here — chapters, the blocks each needs, what gets formalised — is upstream of everything else in the diagram and is never revisited: Gateway_ReviewOutcome's 'iterate' branch re-enters Lane_Agent's Task_AuthorBlocks directly, not this lane, so a scoping mistake made here surfaces only as churn several lanes downstream."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:158
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reviewer's call after step 8. `iterate` returns to authoring with the feedback; `approved` goes to publish."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Typeset the paper through LaTeX to PDF and HTML. Run latex_preflight first — missing packages, fonts or engine — rather than discovering them twenty minutes in. The preamble, class and macros belong to the folio, never to the platform."
msgstr ""

#: processes/authoring-a-paper.bpmn:45
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan — beans (shared by humans and agents)"
msgstr ""
